<title>UK: Hays tumbles after results.</title>
<headline>Hays tumbles after results.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Hays Plc tumbled to their lowest level in almost two months after the group released its interim results.</p>
<p>By 0858 GMT, the shares were down 10-1/2p to 540-1/2, although turnover was light with only 27,735 shares changing hands.  </p>
<p>Hays posted pre-tax pre-exceptional profits of 71.7 million stg for the six months ended December 31.</p>
<p>Dealers said the figure was only slightly weaker than expected.</p>
<p>&quot;It wasn't the figures, it was the quality of the figures that put (the shares) out of favour,&quot; said one market maker.</p>
<p>He noted that a large proportion of the group's profits were generated by its personnel division and did not seem to expand to other units.</p>
<p>--London newsroom +44 171 542 5106</p>
